cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BeamZ in your research, please cite this software.
  When available, cite the Zenodo DOI for the version you used.
type: software
title: "BeamZ: CUDA-accelerated Differentiable FDTD for Photonics"
authors:
  - family-names: Wach
    given-names: Quentin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-7731-890X"
version: "0.5.1"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  BeamZ is an open-source electromagnetic simulation framework for photonic
  design using the finite-difference time-domain (FDTD) method. It provides
  CUDA-accelerated simulations, a Python API, and differentiable workflows
  for gradient-based inverse design of photonic devices.
keywords:
  - FDTD
  - electromagnetics
  - photonics
  - CUDA
  - GPU acceleration
  - inverse design
  - differentiable simulation
repository-code: "https://github.com/beamzorg/beamz"
url: "https://www.beamz.tech"
